wb-cli (0.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Human-mode output. By default `wb-cli` now picks between JSON and a
    compact table/key-value view based on whether stdout is a TTY:
      - SSH without `-t`, pipes, scripts -> JSON (unchanged).
      - Interactive terminal -> human-friendly tables.
    Override anywhere with `--json` / `--human` or `WB_CLI_OUTPUT=json|human`.
    LLM agents are encouraged to pass `--json` explicitly.
  * New `wb_cli/render.py` with generic table / key-value / JSON-fallback
    rendering; each plugin can override via `BasePlugin.render(result)`.
  * Spinner on stderr for every command (`auto_spinner` per plugin;
    modbus scan keeps its own ProgressBar). Silent when stderr is not a
    TTY or when `WB_CLI_NO_SPINNER` is set.
  * `wb-cli <plugin>` with no subcommand now prints that plugin's help
    instead of returning an empty `{"data": {}}`.
  * devices set: refuses to publish to a control that isn't visible on
    the broker (typos like `wb-mr6c_52` used to silently report ok=true)
    and refuses writes to readonly controls.
  * devices get <device> <control>: new subcommand returning value, type,
    and readonly flag in one call.
  * Tests: full coverage of error paths in lib/mqtt, lib/rpc, lib/job,
    lib/journal; modbus probe/template/device-info/add-devices;
    serial-debug's restore-after-failure; render.auto_render shapes;
    CLI output-mode resolution. 123 tests total.

 -- Wiren Board Team <info@wirenboard.com>  Mon, 11 May 2026 19:30:00 +0000

wb-cli (0.1.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * `wb-cli` with no arguments now prints the top-level help (was silent).
  * modbus scan: wait for the *regular* bus scan to finish — wb-device-manager
    replays the previous *extended* scan first, which used to make us return
    a stale 3-device snapshot instead of the full 8+ device list. Also shows
    a progress bar on TTY, drops `"port": null` from the envelope, and turns
    a missing `mosquitto_sub` into MQTT_BROKER_DOWN instead of a stack trace.
  * mqtt read: reject wildcards (`+`, `#`) — use `mqtt list` for those.
  * rules load <name>: raise RULES_NOT_FOUND when the file is missing, not
    a generic RPC_ERROR_RESPONSE.
  * serial-debug: actually wait `--seconds` before reading the journal
    (previously returned the last 500 unrelated lines instantly); show
    a count-up timer while waiting.
  * job wait: show a spinner so it doesn't look frozen.
  * cloud: hint points to `systemctl start ...`, not a non-existent
    `wb-cli systemd` subcommand.
  * Internals: clean up dead `if ctx.controller` branches, extract scan
    timing constants, ensure the scan subprocess is reaped after terminate.

 -- Wiren Board Team <info@wirenboard.com>  Mon, 11 May 2026 18:30:00 +0000

wb-cli (0.1.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * modbus scan: drop retained "stale" state from a prior scan, stop and
    settle before starting, and wait for genuine progress before accepting
    progress=100 — fixes early returns with only the first few devices.
  * modbus probe: report found=false when wb-mqtt-serial returns an empty
    response (previously reported every empty address as a hit).
  * Documentation: collapse DECISIONS.md and CLAUDE.md into README.md, add a
    Skills section with the install-skills.sh matrix.
  * install-skills.sh: new "manual --dest <dir>" target; --dest available
    for claude/opencode too; embedded usage help.

 -- Wiren Board Team <info@wirenboard.com>  Mon, 11 May 2026 17:45:00 +0000

